+## Page-share counters
+
+Software-attention page-share instrumentation is available in builds configured
+with `cmake -B gen --preset native -DTRON_PAGE_SHARE_COUNTERS=ON` (also enabled by
+the `coverage` preset). After rebuilding, set the environment variable
+`TRON_PAGE_SHARE_COUNTERS=1` before starting runtron or rinzler. Only the exact
+value `1` enables collection; unset, `0`, and every other value disable it. The
+setting is cached on first use for the lifetime of the process.
+
+Both binaries register these read-only, casual leaves under
+`<mountpoint>/rinzler/stats/page_share/` before mounting the stats tree:
+
+| Leaf | Cumulative value |
+|------|------------------|
+| `page_visits` | Visits to a (KV page, KV head) with at least one relevant query token |
+| `relevant_query_tokens` | Query-token/page-visit pairs with at least one relevant key |
+| `shared_visits` | Visits with at least two relevant query tokens |
+| `shared_tokens` | Query-token/page-visit pairs from shared visits |
+| `pending_visits` | Counted visits in the second (pending) attention pass |
+| `histogram` | JSON array of visit counts for 1, 2, 3, 4, 5–8, 9–16, and >16 relevant query tokens, in that order |
+
+Read a total with `cat <mountpoint>/rinzler/stats/page_share/page_visits`.
+Subtract an earlier read from a later read to measure an interval; histogram
+slots can be subtracted the same way. There is no reset file. Each atomic is
+read separately and a flush updates several atomics, so live reads do not form
+a consistent snapshot across totals and histogram slots. Values describe visits
+and sharing opportunities, not measured page-load savings.
+
+With runtime collection disabled, instrumented binaries still expose all six
+leaves: the totals stay zero and the histogram is `[0,0,0,0,0,0,0]`. With the CMake
+option OFF (the default), both the hooks and leaves are absent. The build gate
+remains until the whole-host performance controls in
+[#4303](https://github.com/positron-ai/tron/issues/4303) establish that compiling
+runtime-disabled hooks into every build has no measurable cost.
+
+These leaves are for manual inspection and are not exported to Prometheus.
+The existing `[page-share]` stderr summary is retained at normal process exit
+when any visit was counted, providing final totals after the FUSE tree has been
+unmounted. No summary is printed when collection recorded no visits.
+
